   276	## 4. Negative direction (A)
   277	
   278	**Theorem N (proved; union bound and Brun–Titchmarsh).** Let L be any set of primes in
   279	(Y, 16Y] with 16Y ≤ P^{θ}, θ < 1/2, and let V be any weight set. Put
   280	λ = |V|·Σ_{ℓ∈L} 1/(ℓ−1). Then
   281	
   282	  #{covered pairs of S_n} ≤ (2/(1−θ) + o(1))·λ·|S_n|.
   283	
   284	*Proof.*
   285	- For fixed (A, B, ℓ) and a prime p, the partners q with ℓ | Bp − Aq form one class mod ℓ
   286	  in the interval I_p of q-values.
   287	- Montgomery–Vaughan's Brun–Titchmarsh gives ≤ 2|I_p|/(φ(ℓ) log(|I_p|/ℓ)).
   288	- For all but O(P^{0.99}) primes p we have |I_p| ≥ P^{0.99}, and those exceptional p
   289	  contribute o(|S_n|) in total.
   290	- Summing over p and comparing with |S_n| = (1 + o(1))Σ_p |I_p|/log P (PNT on each I_p)
   291	  gives the bound. ∎
   292	
