The extraction argument looks sound so far: the order pre-step makes the babies distinct modulo each prime, and the true giant’s path then yields either a factor or the exact value \(Bp+Aq\). I found two issues to investigate further: the code scans past the stated order threshold, and T2’s CRT density argument does not justify its claimed bound on how many classes can be prescribed.
