codex
The \(N^{1/5}\) corollary and the conditional \(N^{1/6+o(1)}\) corollary survive the audit. I found a separate cost omission for arbitrary weight lists: the algorithm pays to test rejected weight–prime combinations, but those attempts are absent from the bound. T2’s “at most six primes” claim has a concrete counterexample; its CRT density calculation is valid only on the complete residue space, not as an existence bound for pairs of the required size.
